   "built" -> "{2026, 9, 7, 23, 6, 43.509338}", 
    "history" -> {"2.0.0", "", "", ""}, "context" -> "MagneticTB`", 
    "keywords" -> {
     "kagome", "noncollinear antiferromagnet", "induced spinor", 
      "Brillouin zone", "standard k path"}, "specialkeywords" -> {}, 
    "tutorialcollectionlinks" -> {}, "index" -> True, "label" -> 
    "Magnetic T B Tech Note", "language" -> "en", "paclet" -> "MagneticTB", 
    "status" -> "None", "summary" -> 
    "MagneticTB help home Use a kagome antiferromagnet to draw the crystal \
structure, its magnetic moments, and the first Brillouin zone. The three \
in-plane moments are 120 degrees apart. After setting up this model, we \
obtain a k path and use it to plot the three bands. Choose magnetic space \
group 191.239, P6'/m'mm', with a = 1 and c = 4. One representative atom \
generates {1/2,0,0}, {0,1/2,0}, and {1/2,1/2,0}, in this order. Their moments \
in the lattice-vector basis are {1,0,0}, {0,1,0}, and {-1,-1,0}. In Cartesian \
coordinates, these are unit vectors 120 degrees apart and their sum is zero.",
     "synonyms" -> {}, "tabletags" -> {}, "title" -> 
